# Keep the host's build artefacts out of the image.
#
# The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and then `COPY . .`. Without this file that copy
# puts the host's node_modules on top of the ones just installed in the image —
# and npm installs platform-specific binaries, so a tree built on macOS lands
# darwin-arm64 esbuild and rollup in a linux container and the Vite build fails
# on an error that says nothing about where the files came from.
#
# It also keeps roughly 170 MB out of the build context, which is the difference
# between a fast build and one that spends most of its time uploading.
node_modules
dist
.vite

# Local environment and editor state, which should never be baked into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# Nothing in the image needs version control history.
.git
.gitignore
